-- test: ADR 0067 amendment (2026-10-06), A19_fn_result_T_choice: a T value decided by comparing T values goes where a value of T is expected (a lambda, a higher-order function, a function result, an `edit` binding or a field of the body), which edition 0.2 rejects in the generic body; the leak is rejected there, an accepted cost, since accepting it soundly would need re-checking lambdas (spec/07 §7 rule 8, #92)
-- spec: spec/07 §7
-- expect: error U4001 at src/a19_fn_result_t_choice.una:6:58
module a19_fn_result_t_choice

mk[T](a: T, b: T, p: T, q: T) -> fn(Int) -> T = fn(n) -> if a == b then p else q

pub leak(s: secret Int) -> Int = mk([s], b: [0], p: [], q: [1, 2])(0).len
